<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/060G">Corollary <span data-tag="060G">8.5.6.15</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a pullback diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [r]^-{F} \ar [d]^{U} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' \ar [d]^{U'} \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r]^-{ \overline{F} } &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}', } \]
</div>
<p> where the vertical maps are right fibrations. If $\overline{F}$ is a Morita equivalence, then $F$ is a Morita equivalence. </p>
